1747 RX replyinfo motd\nWelcome to Crossfire!\n\nThis is a test server for the Crossfire Web Client.\nDon't expect stability...\n\nIn the WebClient, the [b]Alt[/b] key is used instead [b]CTRL[/b] for running.\n\n\nTo report bugs, create an issue at:\nhttps://github.com/bofh69/crossfire-web-client/\n\x00
1751 RX replyinfo news\n%2026-05-30 Updated client\n\n* There is a simple keyboard UI navigation support.\n  Bind 'ui_nav' to a key, then navigate with cursor keys, tab, enter and escape.\n* Big face handling together with Fog of War has been updated a lot.\n  There are still rendering artifacts, but they should be alot fewer.\n* Grayscale Fog of War now keeps some color.\n* Restore/Import of config has been fixed.\n* Preformatted text is handled better in the InfoPanel.\n\n%2026-05-18 Updated client & server\n\n* Fixes for zooming in.\n* CTRL + scrollwheel can now be used on the map for zooming as well.\n* If the URL has a \"record=1\", the websocket communication is stored in the client and new menu entries are in the Connection menu for handling it.\n* There is a /replay.html page for (re)rendering the websocket communication for the server.\n\n* The arches, maps and server are updated to latest versions.\n\n%2026-05-18 Updated client\n\n* Added tooltips when hovering over items.\n\n%2026-05-17 Updated client\n\n* Magic map is fixed again...\n* Improved memory usage\n\nThe client now supports [fixed]fixed[print], [arcane]arcane[print], [hand]hand[print] and [strange]strange[print] fonts.\n\n\n%2026-05-15 Updated client\n\n* Pickup menu's checkboxes were not set during login.\n\n* Delay rendering if faces's bitmaps are being created.\n\n* Add support for changing faceset\n\n%2026-05-13 Updated client\n\n* Its possible to right click on text in the info panel, then change the filter for its group\nor split the info panel in two, one with that type and one without.\n\n* The hotbar wasn't visible unless one added something to one of its slots. Now it should be\nvisible as long as at least one slot is used.\n\n* The colors used in the info panel can be configured.\n\n* Its possible to store the config to a file and restore it from a file.\n\n* When receiving dialog texts, they are slightly filtered and buttons will be added\nto the info panel for sending answers.\n\n\n%2026-05-07 Updated client\n\n* Stats' headings are fixed.\n\n* Fixed big face/tile drawing order.\n\n* Hotbar is only shown when used.\n\n* Resizing the window should more often keep the map content, ignoring the server's newmap.\n\n\n%2026-05-06 Updated client\n\n* Renamed Help menu to Info.\n\n* Added hiscore menu item.\n\n* Made the client almost usable on mobile browsers:\n  One can move around with long presses.\n  The ground items are not visible in horizontal mode,\n  some dialog boxes are too wide for vertical mode...\n  Commands can be input, so chat is possible.\n\n\n%2026-05-04 Updated client\n\nUses interpolation for darkness values and graying for fog of war.\nBy default graying is turned off for firefox as it doesn't use\nhardware acceleration for the filter operation. On faster computers\nit still works well, so turn it on in the Config menu.\n\n\n%2026-04-30 Updated client\n\n* Hotbar reload fixes. Neither tag nor face is stable accross logins so\n  the hotbar will now use the first item with the same name to get the face nr.\n\n* Fix min/max stats for character creation.\n\n* Improved performance when overloaded.\n\n\n%2026-04-29 Updated client & server\n\nServer updated so more than one character can be created via web sockets...\n\nImproved magic mapping command.\n\nResized UI sligthly for smaller screens.\n\nIcons for filtering inventory and messages.\n\n\n%2026-04-25 Updated client\n\nLots of minor fixes and improvements.\n\nHotbar & key/button bindings are now stored per character.\nThe key/button dialogs can be used to make each binding global again.\n\nSome of the UI elements can be resized.\n\nQuest and knowledge lists have their own tabs now.\n\nAll skills info is shown now (base/race/applied).\n\nThere is a local \"debug\" command to help debug bigface/tile issues and more.\n\n\n%2026-04-11 Updated client\n\nGamepads can be used.\n\nA hotbar has been added, bind \"hotbar\" to\na gamepad button for selecting slots. Right click on\nitems, skills and spells to add them to the slots.\nThe keyboard menu has an entry for arbitrary commands.\n\nSmoothing is enabled.\n\nThe input field now supports command history and tab completion.\n\nMove-to works (right click on tile).\n\nPossible to zoom in/out in the map.\n\n%2026-04-13 Updated client\n\nClient accepts server parameter with the server's websocket address:\nie https://crossfire.diegeekdie.com/?server=wss://example.com/ws\n\nSome bug fixes\n\n\n%2026-04-05 Server installed\n\nThis is the beginning of a fantastic journey.\n\x00
1764 RX replyinfo rules\n\n[i]Behavior[/i]\nPlease keep conversations on the shout and chat channels friendly.\n\n[i]Bugs[/i]\nDo not exploit bugs. If you come across one, please report it.\n\n[i]Player Killing[/i]\nPlayer killing is not allowed unless both players agree to it.\n\n[i]Stealing[/i]\nDo not steal items from other players.\n\n[b]All violations are punishable at the discretion of the dungeon master.[/b]\n\x00
